%% D5. Missing-data considerations
%% A guide to reasoning, not an automatic rule for choosing a model.
flowchart TD
  A["Describe the missingness: intermittent visits, dropout, missing covariates; by arm and over time"] --> B["Why could data be missing? Use design and clinical knowledge, not only the data"]
  B --> C{"Is MAR plausible given variables you can use?"}
  C -->|"Yes, and they are in the analysis model"| D["Likelihood-based LMM or GLMM on all observed data"]
  C -->|"Yes, but GEE is planned"| E["Standard GEE needs MCAR or covariate-dependent missingness: use weighted GEE or multiple imputation"]
  C -->|"Yes, via auxiliary variables not in the analysis model"| F["Multiple imputation with auxiliary variables, respecting the longitudinal structure"]
  D --> G["Avoid LOCF and complete-case analysis as the primary approach"]
  E --> G
  F --> G
  G --> H["MNAR cannot be ruled out from the data: sensitivity analysis with delta adjustment and a tipping point"]
  H --> I["Is visit timing related to the outcome? Consider the visit process (Module 10)"]
  classDef q fill:#ffffff,stroke:#555555,color:#222222;
  classDef m fill:#eef4f8,stroke:#0b5d8f,color:#222222;
  class A,B,C,I q;
  class D,E,F,G,H m;
